    "type": "Collection",
    "id": "ostia-sst-reprocessed-climate",
    "stac_version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "The OSTIA reprocessed sea surface temperature product provides a consistent, climate-quality data record spanning from 1982 to present. This dataset uses the same OSTIA analysis system as the operational product but applies it to reprocessed satellite observations and quality-controlled in situ data. The reprocessing ensures temporal consistency and homogeneity, making it ideal for climate studies, trend analysis, and long-term monitoring of Southern Ocean temperatures. The product maintains 0.05° spatial resolution and daily temporal resolution throughout the entire record. This Climate Data Record (CDR) is particularly valuable for studying Antarctic sea ice-ocean interactions, marine heatwave detection, and validating climate models over multi-decadal timescales.",
